  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1256 AM CST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nA strong shortwave will move into the region this evening, with\nrain developing and moving into the area overnight. The rain will\ncontinue overnight through much of Wednesday. Rainfall amounts \nwill vary, ranging from just a few hundreds over the west to 1.5 \nto 2.0 inches in the east. The rain will end from west to east \nThursday afternoon into the evening hours. With the recent drought\nconditions and long duration of this rainfall, we do not expect \nany flooding concerns.\n\nExpect mainly dry and cool conditions on Thanksgiving day with \nhighs mostly in the low 50s. Temperatures will drop to around \nfreezing Thursday nigh across the entire area. The cool and dry \nconditions will continue through Friday, with a warmup on Saturday\nout ahead of another short wave that will bring more rain on \nSunday into Sunday night. /15/",
